# Trivy suppressions.
#
# The bar for an entry here is high on purpose: a suppression is a decision that a finding will
# NOT be fixed, and an unexplained one is indistinguishable from a finding nobody looked at. Every
# entry states the vulnerability, why it is unfixable rather than merely inconvenient, why it is
# not reachable in this project, and what would make it removable. Anything that can be fixed is
# fixed instead -- see docs/security/audit.md for the full disposition of every open finding.
#
# Format: one vulnerability ID per line. Trivy also accepts `exp:` for a dated expiry; none is used
# here because these are conditions that change on an upstream event, not on a date.

# CVE-2025-14505 / GHSA-848j-6mx2-7j84 -- elliptic <= 6.6.1, "Uses a Cryptographic Primitive with a
# Risky Implementation" (CVSS 5.6, LOW). ECDSA signing can truncate the nonce `k` when its interim
# value has leading zeros, which under repetition can leak the private key.
#
# NO FIX EXISTS. Every published version of elliptic is in the vulnerable range and the advisory
# lists no patched version, so this cannot be resolved by a bump. It is not a version this project
# chose or pinned.
#
# NOT REACHABLE HERE. elliptic is not a dependency of this project; it arrives transitively:
#
#     crypto-browserify@3.12.1
#     |- browserify-sign@4.2.6 -> elliptic@6.6.1
#     `- create-ecdh@4.0.4     -> elliptic@6.6.1
#
# and `crypto-browserify` exists solely as a webpack browser polyfill for Node's `crypto`
# (webpack.config.js: `"crypto": require.resolve("crypto-browserify")`). The MCP server runs on
# Node, where `crypto` resolves to the built-in module and the alias is never applied. Nothing
# under src/ imports elliptic, browserify-sign or create-ecdh directly, and no operation performs
# ECDSA signing through them.
#
# REMOVABLE WHEN: elliptic publishes a fixed release, or `crypto-browserify` is dropped along with
# the vestigial web build (which would be the better outcome -- this fork removed the web app in
# v1.7.1 and the webpack browser aliases are the last thing keeping the dependency alive).
CVE-2025-14505
